# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the build output and applies it at the edge.
#
# This app renders model output, and the model repeats what a learner types, so
# the policy assumes that content is hostile. connect-src names the API and the
# agent explicitly: an injected fetch to anywhere else is refused by the browser
# even if it reaches the DOM. Cloudflare Web Analytics loads its beacon script
# and posts to cloudflareinsights.com. frame-src names the API because the
# tutor's cards are MCP Apps views, framed in a sandbox the API serves.
#
# Google sign-in (Firebase, by popup): the SDK loads Google's frame helper from
# apis.google.com and frames the project's auth domain, which passes the popup's
# result back; it signs in and refreshes tokens at identitytoolkit and
# securetoken.
#
# Voice lessons record from the microphone on this origin only, and play the
# teacher's voice from blob: URLs made of what the API sent.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; media-src 'self' blob:; script-src 'self' 'sha256-OEmWuvXkuK9AZVySRHk13IirFWS83AUGIYi63KpmXY8=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://apis.google.com; connect-src 'self' https://graspy-api.getlatentic.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com; frame-src https://graspy-api.getlatentic.com https://graspy-f482e.firebaseapp.com

# The service worker is always checked for a new version: a stale one would
# serve a stale app.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
